Kigali Fleet Storefront — Complete Customer Experience & Product Specification 🚗
We are now designing one of the most commercially important parts of Kigali Fleet: the public booking storefront that a transport company shares with its customers.
I want you to think about this from the customer's perspective, not the developer's perspective.
Imagine you own a car rental company in Kigali. You register your business on Kigali Fleet, add your vehicles, and receive a personalized booking link.
You share that link with:
•	A tourist planning a Rwanda safari.
•	An NGO arranging transport for its staff.
•	A corporate employee visiting Kigali.
•	A local customer who needs a vehicle for three days.
•	Someone arriving at Kigali International Airport.
When they open your link, they should experience a professional booking service that makes them comfortable enough to trust your company, select a vehicle, make a booking and pay.
The storefront must sell the transport company's services, not Kigali Fleet's software.
That distinction is fundamental.
