2. The storefront's primary objectives
A successful storefront must accomplish six things:
Objective	Customer outcome
Discovery	Understand what the company offers
Trust	Believe the company is legitimate
Selection	Find the right vehicle or service
Booking	Submit an accurate reservation
Payment	Pay through supported methods
Confirmation	Know exactly what happens next
If a customer cannot understand the service, verify the business, calculate the cost, or understand what happens after booking, the storefront has failed.
