PART 15 — My final product recommendation
I see three products inside this one storefront concept:
Product 1
Business website
A transport company gets a professional public website to showcase its identity, fleet and services.
Product 2
Booking engine
Customers discover, configure, request, reserve and pay for transport services.
Product 3
Customer relationship and communication system
The business handles confirmations, support, customer history, changes, payments and repeat bookings.
All three should work together.
The storefront should not become an independent website disconnected from the company's fleet and booking management system.
For example:
•	A vehicle becomes unavailable in the company dashboard → it disappears from available search results.
•	A company changes a published price → the new price appears on the storefront.
•	A customer submits a booking → the company sees it in its dashboard.
•	A dispatcher assigns a driver → the customer receives the appropriate update.
•	A payment is verified → the booking's payment status changes.
•	A vehicle enters maintenance → it cannot be booked for conflicting dates.
That synchronization is what makes this a real Fleet Management SaaS.
